  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (RNA, multi-profile, PCA, avgpool) is the current best at 0.591 acc, substantially outperforming single-profile RNA (0.485), transformer aggregation (0.519), and image-only ResNet50 (0.208). This establishes multi-profile + avgpool as the strongest RNA configuration and suggests the image modality (ResNet50) is currently a weak signal. Uncertainty: whether PCA_n2000 is the best RNA representation, or whether a purpose-built learned encoder (scvi) could further improve performance in this optimal multi-profile/avgpool setup. Question tested: config_005 changes only the RNA encoder from PCA to scvi_n200 while keeping multi-profile and avgpool fixed, giving a clean single-variable comparison to config_002. Why best next step: It directly exploits the strongest known direction (multi-profile + avgpool) while probing the most impactful remaining design choice (RNA encoder quality). The result will determine whether to invest further in RNA encoder upgrades or pivot to multimodal/fusion experiments, and it avoids the low-information risk of adding a weak image modality before confirming the RNA backbone is well-optimized."
}

